Project Overview
Project Name: Shopeasy Customer App

Repository Name: customer_ordereasy_njs

Framework: Next.js 14 (App Router)

Language: TypeScript

Styling: Tailwind CSS

Purpose: This is the customer-facing web application for the "Shopeasy" platform. It allows users to browse retailers, manage carts, place orders, and track loyalty rewards.

Key Features
The application includes a comprehensive suite of e-commerce features tailored for a multi-retailer platform:

Retailer Selection: Users can browse and select from available shops and categories.

Product Browsing: Features an optimized grid view layout with search capabilities.

Cart & Checkout: Full cycle management for adding items to the cart and placing orders.

User Authentication: Supports Login/Signup functionality, specifically mentioning OTP (One-Time Password) verification.

Address & Location: Integrated Google Maps for precise location picking and address management.

Loyalty & Rewards: Includes a referral system and tracking for loyalty points.

Technical Stack & Architecture
Core Framework: Next.js 14 (Utilizing the modern App Router architecture).

Styling: Tailwind CSS for utility-first, responsive design.

Language: TypeScript (Ensures type safety and better developer experience).

State/API Management: Likely uses React Hooks for local state and standard Fetch/Axios for API calls (implied by the services directory).

External Integrations:

Google Maps API: For location services.

Custom Backend API: Connects to api.ordereasy.win.

Project Structure
The project follows the standard Next.js App Router structure inside the src directory:

src/app: Contains the App Router pages, layouts, and route groups.

src/components: Reusable UI components (buttons, inputs, product cards, etc.).

src/services: API service configurations and HTTP client setups.

public: Static assets like images and icons.

Installation & Setup Guide
1. Prerequisites
Node.js: v18 or higher

npm: v9 or higher

2. Installation
Bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/vin8003/customer_ordereasy_njs.git

# Navigate to the directory
cd customer_ordereasy_njs

# Install dependencies
npm install
3. Environment Configuration
You must create a .env.local file in the root directory to configure the app.

Bash
# Create the file
touch .env.local
Required Environment Variables:

Code snippet
# Backend API Endpoint
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.ordereasy.win/api/

# Google Maps API Key (Required for Location Picker)
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here
4. Running the Project
Development: npm run dev (Runs on http://localhost:3000)

Production Build: npm run build

Start Production Server: npm start